// Customer-run relays ("bring your own compute"), enrolled on the overlay.
//
// A customer's relay never holds a MOQOM credential. It holds an OpenZiti
// identity, enrolled once with the one-time token this API hands out, and the
// control plane maps that identity to one tenant. The relay dials out to the
// control plane over the overlay, so the customer opens no inbound port, and
// MOQOM opens no port to the customer either.
//
// The enrolment is the licence. Revoking it deletes the overlay identity, which
// stops the relay reaching the control plane, and cuts the stream it already
// has: no more directives, no more verification keys, so the client tokens it
// could check stop being ones it can check once they rotate.
//
// Internal for now, beside the relay link, and served only on the overlay API
// service. Whether it joins the public admin API is an open question in
// docs/OPENZITI-AND-P2P.md.

